As expected, the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/07/28/apple-upgrade-program-klarna/">Apple Upgrade program launched today</a>, allowing customers in the U.S. to lease most iPhone, Apple Watch, iPad, and Mac models. While the program is offered by Apple, the leasing is handled by financing company Klarna.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/07/Apple-Upgrade-iPhone.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1057827" /><br/>
The program essentially allows you to subscribe to an Apple device with monthly payments. At the end of the lease, you can return your device and either upgrade to a new one or move on. If you prefer to own your device at the end of the lease, you can pay an amount equal to the retail price minus any lease payments made to Klarna.<br/>
<br/>
No matter which option you choose at the end of your lease, you will never pay more than the retail price of the device, according to Apple.<br/>
<br/>
Apple Upgrade allows you to lease an iPhone for as little as &#36;17.99 per month, with the complete breakdown of starting prices listed below.<br/>
<br/>
